<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-S3-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-S3-003" ;
  triage:title "#[cfg(not(unix))] prepare_local_ipc_endpoint stub is silent no-op without explanatory comment (local_ipc_transport.rs:454)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport.rs:454 — the #[cfg(not(unix))] arm of prepare_local_ipc_endpoint is a silent no-op. cross-platform-guidelines.md requires explicit documentation of every OS-specific seam. A comment is required explaining that Windows named-pipe endpoints are OS-managed and require no pre-creation or stale-socket removal. Fix is comment-only. Note: ATM-QA-S2-013 covers the same pattern at local_ipc_transport.rs:395 on feature/pS-s2-windows-ipc — TASK-1148 fixed that occurrence on S.2. Verify whether the S.2 merge-forward at 9698a17 brought this fix to S.3 (may already be closed). (quality-mgr reported as ATM-QA-NEW-001 in S.3 QA-2 report.)" ;
